{"type":"message","id":"0fbc1847","parentId":"1c544296","timestamp":"2026-09-26T22:43:33.340Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"### Verified Reliability Across the OpenRouter `:free` Roster\n\nCommunity testing across OpenRouter's live catalog shows that older free staples (DeepSeek R1, Llama 3.3 70B, Qwen3 Coder) have rotated off the free list.\n\nThe primary failure mode on free endpoints is **upstream provider rate-limiting (429s)**:\n\n* **Google's Gemma 4 endpoints** (`google/gemma-4-31b-it:free`) consistently bounce back upstream 429s under standard community load.\n* **Poolside models** (`poolside/laguna-s-2.1:free`) have frequent upstream 429s or drop empty HTTP 200 responses.\n* **Thinking Machines models** (`thinkingmachines/inkling:free`) throw 403s on standard API completions unless wrapped in an active agent harness.\n\n---\n\n### The #1 Model You Can Rely On\n\n#### **`nvidia/nemotron-3-super-120b-a12b:free`** (or `nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free`)\n\n* **Why it works reliably:** NVIDIA funds and provisions dedicated enterprise inference infrastructure directly through OpenRouter. It exhibits the lowest upstream refusal rate and highest daily completion consistency across community tracker runs.\n* **Capabilities:** 262k context window, hybrid Mamba-Transformer MoE architecture, strong native tool/function calling, and stable streaming.\n* **Caveat:** Leave plenty of headroom in `max_tokens` (do not constrain it to `<500`), as Nemotron models emit internal reasoning tokens before outputting code or final text.\n\n---\n\n### The Resilient Fallback Strategy\n\nSingle free endpoints are inherently subject to provider capacity shifts. The standard production-grade configuration uses an automated fallback chain in your client or proxy config:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"models\": [\n    \"nvidia/nemotron-3-super-120b-a12b:free\",\n    \"nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free\",\n    \"openrouter/free\"\n  ]\n}\n\n```\n\n* **`openrouter/free`:** OpenRouter's built-in dynamic routing meta-endpoint. If a specific model's upstream nodes are temporarily saturated with 429s, `openrouter/free` automatically routes the request to whichever free endpoint currently has idle capacity.\n\n---\n\n### Operational Check\n\nBefore running any free model, verify:\n\n1. **Balance Check:** Even for `:free` models, if your OpenRouter account balance is **negative** (from past paid runs), the gateway rejects all requests with `402 Payment Required`.\n2. **Rate Caps:** Unfunded accounts have a hard ceiling of **20 requests/minute and 50 requests/day**. If your agent loops or polls faster than ~3 seconds between turns, you will trigger gateway throttles."}],"steering":true,"attribution":"user","timestamp":1790462611137}}
