{"type":"message","id":"79399c44","parentId":"fce5f455","timestamp":"2026-09-26T22:47:18.585Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Let's trace the actual filesystem and git tree to see what's actually there before touching anything:\n\n```bash\ncd ~/sovereign/projects/range/ranch/stockyard/tau\n\n# Check both packages/utils and any pi-utils directories/symlinks\nls -d packages/*utils* 2>/dev/null\n\n# Find where dirs.ts actually lives and exports VERSION\nfind packages/ -name \"dirs.ts\" -exec grep -Hn \"VERSION\" {} +\n\n```\n\n### The Two Version Systems In The Repo\n\nIf you're seeing \"both,\" here is the mechanical split across this codebase:\n\n1. **The Static Semver Contract (`base: \"18.3.0\"`):**\n* Stored in `package.json` across packages (`@oh-my-pi/pi-utils`, `@oh-my-pi/pi-coding-agent`, etc.).\n* Bun workspaces and internal `workspace:*` dependency resolvers rely on strict semver string matches (`18.3.0`) so packages can bind to each other without tripping semver range errors.\n\n\n2. **The Dynamic Build Hash Sentinel (`canonical: \"tau/main-18.3.0-sovereign-tau-d83c686c\"`):**\n* Generated during `build-binary.ts` / git hooks into `packages/coding-agent/src/generated/version.json` (and `packages/natives/native/version-sentinel.d.ts`).\n* Used for runtime telemetry, CLI banner reporting, diagnostic logs, and plugin doctor checks.\n\n\n\n---\n\n### Making Both First-Class Without Breaking Workspace Resolution\n\nIf `package.json` version strings get set to `tau/main-18.3.0-...`, Bun will choke on semver comparisons when doing workspace resolution. The proper pattern is to keep clean semver in `package.json`, but export **both** on the runtime object so the CLI and plugins display and verify the hashed git descriptor.\n\nCheck how `dirs.ts` is structured:\n\n```bash\npython3 -c '\nimport glob\n\nmatches = glob.glob(\"packages/**/dirs.ts\", recursive=True)\nfor m in matches:\n    print(\"Found:\", m)\n    with open(m) as f:\n        for line in f:\n            if \"VERSION\" in line:\n                print(\"  \", line.strip())\n'\n\n```\n\nTo give you both cleanly:\n\n```typescript\n// in packages/utils/src/dirs.ts (or wherever dirs.ts resolves)\nimport versionData from \"../../coding-agent/src/generated/version.json\" with { type: \"json\" };\n\n// 1. Strict semver for tooling/bun\nexport const SEMVER_VERSION = versionData.base || \"18.3.0\";\n\n// 2. First-class hashed canonical descriptor for CLI/telemetry/logging\nexport const CANONICAL_VERSION = versionData.canonical || versionData.npm || SEMVER_VERSION;\n\n// Primary VERSION export points to the canonical hashed build\nexport const VERSION = CANONICAL_VERSION;\n\n```\n\nThis gives you the full SHA identity everywhere in the UI and banners (`tau/main-18.3.0-sovereign-tau-d83c686c`) without breaking standard semver requirements in Bun's dependency engine."}],"steering":true,"attribution":"user","timestamp":1790462835274}}
